\DOC ENSURES_WHILE_UP2_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_WHILE_UP2_TAC : term -> term -> term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Reduces an {ensures} goal about a program containing a counted up-loop to a
single subgoal conjoining a nonzero-trip-count condition, a loop-entry
{ensures}, a universally quantified loop-body {ensures}, and a loop-exit
{ensures}, all under the original assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes four terms: a trip count {t} (a numeral or an arbitrary
numeric term), program-counter terms {u1} and {u2} giving the loop-head and
loop-exit addresses, and an invariant {\i s. ...} parameterised by the
iteration index and the machine state.
{
   A ?- ensures step precond postcond frame
   ================================================  ENSURES_WHILE_UP2_TAC t u1 u2 (\i s. ...)
   A ?- t_ne /\ ensures ... /\ (forall x1. ...) /\ ensures ...
}
\noindent The resulting conclusion is a four-way conjunction: first, the
condition that the trip count is nonzero; second, an {ensures} from the
original precondition to the invariant instantiated at index zero, with the
program counter set to the loop-head address {u1}; third, a universally
quantified {ensures} over a fresh index variable {x1}, with hypotheses saying
that the index is below the trip count, that it is not equal to the trip count,
and that the trip count is nonzero and positive, stepping from the invariant at
that index to the invariant at its successor together with a program counter
chosen by a conditional between {u1} and {u2} according to whether the
successor is still below the trip count; and fourth, an {ensures} from the
invariant at the trip count, with the program counter at the loop-exit address
{u2}, to the original postcondition. Each of the three {ensures} components
reuses the state frame {frame} of the original goal unchanged.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single transformation.

\ENDDOC
